{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":true,"decision":"pass","reasons":[],"slug":"tushare-stock-skill","displayName":"TuShare Stock Skill","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/magica-chen/skills/tushare-stock-skill","publisherHandle":"magica-chen","publisherDisplayName":"Zexun Chen","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/magica-chen","version":"1.0.3","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1773097450083,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/tushare-stock-skill/card?ownerHandle=magica-chen&version=1.0.3","sha256":"0f3bce88064e6c09c85b62263ad32cf518e96ea4886d725237ab472a57f7bfad","size":3012,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"adf919d5a9e08607b4a1ca3574a711e62500cc5b93bae764ab1d21f3b3b566d0","bundleFingerprints":["aa9879bfed42d811dd66c889d64a6e61b4849b3a12878baea08a30d7e9298f93","7e282e092397998331db8e96a8b695a94794197b70967aafd650df84a4890ce3"],"files":[{"path":"agents/openai.yaml","size":313,"sha256":"34047a0b9d1f43a091220a8cd8ac18f8691eb2c9e4d6a5e43e4d4d948b4111de","contentType":null},{"path":"README.md","size":5403,"sha256":"4f3924dc32ae788e73a3b578d876fda6c1113c5696ec49e5d4dcee3f3ff2e7b0","contentType":null},{"path":"references/stock_endpoints.json","size":431641,"sha256":"8548687ac64e5919711cf7626e55bef20660bc003cfce75d0873819d743bf7e1","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"references/stock_endpoints.md","size":14296,"sha256":"87937cf72862ba2908706095e8032ef52711882269e57a8ba90b3b515405182d","contentType":null},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":39,"sha256":"595596ba7397a6fd320e4944e4af279a1ae05961deb8a9504bb23b7af995a79e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/build_catalog.py","size":8850,"sha256":"cf3608a39c1f7fc8ffa56ef959d9be437ca55c59006598b98b6db4463df5de1d","contentType":null},{"path":"scripts/trading_analysis.py","size":18581,"sha256":"62c6447bf1ab433b7a0e8f2a11715da7db9a04313192110752a15df9e3390c1f","contentType":null},{"path":"scripts/tushare_stock.py","size":85035,"sha256":"020b60c3a47df54a8d216810b95bbf9503a61996873dea7b5d0e8f3b6fdba4a9","contentType":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6653,"sha256":"2107a848d8af8116bb391eef0cfef0e4a8bc69ee68ad2bfacf7aca36df3956db","contentType":null}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"clean","passed":true,"rawStatus":"clean","verdict":"benign","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a disclosed Tushare stock-research skill that uses a user-provided Tushare token for market-data queries, with some non-blocking hardening issues around dependencies, cache storage, and slightly broad catalog scope.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789132725600,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Predictable and Symlink-Unsafe Shared Cache Path"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/tushare_stock.py"},"region":{"startLine":23,"endLine":23}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"ac774f7279d075b5"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `scripts/tushare_stock.py:23, 474-486, 1727-1732`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unsafe temporary-file and cache handling  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Complete Code Snippet\n\n```python\nCACHE_DIR = Path(os.environ.get(\"TUSHARE_STOCK_CACHE_DIR\", \"/tmp/tushare_stock_skill\"))\n```\n\n```python\ndef cache_path(name: str) -> Path:\n    CACHE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    return CACHE_DIR / name\n\n\ndef load_stock_cache() -> list[dict] | None:\n    path = cache_path(\"stock_basic_cache.json\")\n    if not path.exists():\n        return None\n    age = time_since(path)\n    if age > timedelta(hours=24):\n        return None\n    return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n```\n\n```python\n    if not frames:\n        return []\n    merged = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True).drop_duplicates(subset=[\"ts_code\"])\n    merged = merged.fillna(\"\")\n    rows = merged.to_dict(orient=\"records\")\n    cache_path(\"stock_basic_cache.json\").write_text(json.dumps(rows, ensure_ascii=False), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return rows\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe default cache directory is a predictable, shared path under `/tmp`. The implementation creates the directory with `exist_ok=True` but does not verify:\n\n- Whether the directory is owned by the current user.\n- Whether the directory or cache file is a symbolic link.\n- Whether the cache file is a regular file.\n- Whether directory and file permissions prevent access by other local users.\n- Whether the final write is atomic.\n\nBoth `read_text()` and `write_text()` follow symbolic links. An attacker with local access could pre-create `/tmp/tushare_stock_skill`, place a crafted `stock_basic_cache.json` in it, or arrange a link to another path. The program would then trust the attacker-controlled cache when resolving stock names or follow the selected path during a cache write.\n\nThe cached information is public stock metadata rather than credentials. Consequently, this issue does not directly expose `TUSHARE_TOKEN`, but it creates a local integrity and file-safety weakness.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A local attacker creates `/tmp/tushare_stock_skill` before the victim first runs the Skill and gives the victim sufficient access to traverse or write into it.\n2. The attacker places a malicious `stock_basic_cache.json` in that directory or creates the cache file as a symbolic link.\n3. The victim invokes a natural-language stock query or analysis operation.\n4. `load_stock_cache()` accepts and parses the attacker-controlled file without checking ownership or file type.\n5. The poisoned stock metadata can influence stock-name resolution and cause the Skill to query or analyze an unintended security.\n6. Alternatively, when the cache is refreshed, `write_text()` can follow a symbolic link and overwrite another file that is writable by the victim process.\n\nSuccessful redirection of a write is constrained by the victim process's existing filesystem permissions; this issue does not independently bypass operating-system access controls.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe principal impact is local integrity loss:\n\n- Poisoning of stock-name-to-code resolution.\n- Incorrect market-data queries and misleading financial analysis.\n- Corruption or replacement of another file writable by the victim if a link-based redirection succeeds.\n- Potential denial of service through malformed JSON, unexpected file types, or permission manipulation.\n\nNo direct privilege escalation is established. The maximum filesystem impact remains limited to locations the victim account can already modify.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Replace the shared cache location with a private per-user cache directory, such as one returned by `platformdirs.user_cache_dir()`.\n2. Create the cache directory with mode `0700` and verify that it is owned by the current user.\n3. Reject symbolic links and non-regular files before reading or writing.\n4. Open files using low-level flags such as `O_NOFOLLOW`, where supported, and use mode `0600`.\n5. Write to a securely created temporary file in the same directory, flush and synchronize it, and atomically replace the cache with `os.replace()`.\n6. Validate the JSON schema before trusting cached records.\n7. If `/tmp` must remain the default, use a user-specific directory containing the effective user ID and still perform ownership and link checks.\n8. Handle malformed or untrusted cache data gracefully by discarding it and fetching a fresh copy.\n\nExample hardening direction:\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nCACHE_DIR = Path.home() / \".cache\" / \"tushare_stock_skill\"\n\ndef initialize_cache_dir() -> None:\n    CACHE_DIR.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    stat = CACHE_DIR.lstat()\n    if CACHE_DIR.is_symlink() or stat.st_uid != os.geteuid():\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Unsafe cache directory\")\n\ndef atomic_cache_write(path: Path, content: str) -> None:\n    initialize_cache_dir()\n    fd, temporary_name = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=CACHE_DIR)\n    try:\n        os.fchmod(fd, 0o600)\n        with os.fdopen(fd, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:\n            handle.write(content)\n            handle.flush()\n            os.fsync(handle.fileno())\n        os.replace(temporary_name, path)\n    finally:\n        if os.path.exists(temporary_name):\n            os.unlink(temporary_name)\n```\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Third-Party Dependencies Permit Non-Reproducible Installation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"requirements.txt"},"region":{"startLine":1,"endLine":4}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"9a9180b68d531138"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `requirements.txt:1-4`; installation documented at `SKILL.md:101-103`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned third-party dependencies  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Complete Code Snippet\n\n```text\npandas\ntushare\nrequests\nbeautifulsoup4\n```\n\nThe documented installation command is:\n\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nEvery dependency is specified without a version constraint or integrity hash. Each installation therefore resolves whichever package versions are available from the configured Python package index at that time.\n\nThis makes the installation non-reproducible and increases supply-chain risk. A malicious or compromised future release, compromised package distribution account, unsafe configured package index, or unexpected incompatible update could introduce code that executes during installation or when imported.\n\nThis is particularly relevant because the runtime imports `tushare`, `pandas`, `requests`, and `beautifulsoup4` components. The Tushare dependency also executes in a process that has access to `TUSHARE_TOKEN` during authenticated operations.\n\nNo evidence was found that the currently named dependencies are typosquatted or intentionally malicious. The issue is the absence of version and artifact-integrity controls.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker compromises a dependency release channel, publishes a malicious future release through a compromised maintainer account, or controls an index configured in the victim's pip environment.\n2. The victim follows the documented `pip install -r requirements.txt` instruction.\n3. pip resolves the mutable dependency name to the attacker-controlled or compromised release because no reviewed version is pinned.\n4. Package installation logic may execute with the privileges of the user running pip.\n5. The malicious package may subsequently execute when the Skill imports it.\n6. During normal Skill execution, malicious dependency code could access the process environment, including `TUSHARE_TOKEN`, read files available to the user, alter analysis results, or make unauthorized network requests.\n\nThis exploitation path requires a compromised dependency distribution path or malicious resolved release; the requirements file does not itself provide arbitrary-code execution without such a supply-chain event.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA malicious dependency can execute with the privileges of the installation or runtime process. Depending on how the user installs and runs the Skill, potential scope includes:\n\n- Access to `TUSHARE_TOKEN` and other environment variables visible to the process.\n- Read and write access to files available to the executing user.\n- Unauthorized outbound network communication.\n- Manipulation of retrieved market data and generated financial analysis.\n- Persistence or broader system modification if the user performs installation with elevated privileges.\n\nThe project itself does not request elevated installation privileges, so system-wide compromise is conditional on the user running pip as an administrator or root.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Pin every direct and transitive dependency to a reviewed version.\n2. Generate and verify cryptographic hashes for all approved distributions.\n3. Use a lock-generation workflow such as:\n\n```bash\npip-compile --generate-hashes requirements.in\npip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n4. Review dependency updates through a controlled process rather than accepting mutable latest releases.\n5. Prefer binary wheels from the official package index and restrict pip to explicitly approved indexes.\n6. Avoid running pip with administrative or root privileges.\n7. Use an isolated virtual environment with only the permissions needed by this Skill.\n8. Add automated vulnerability and provenance checks, such as `pip-audit`, dependency review, and software bill-of-materials generation.\n9. Consider separating development-only catalog-building dependencies from runtime dependencies so normal users install the smallest necessary dependency set.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":50,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789132510.8995626,"endTime":1789132656.2103503}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"tushare-stock-skill","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v570awgnty3vcvnm5hvjwrpr3h8e6grv-nwydlp/clawscan-skillspector-355687891/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T13:15:09.650127+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":136,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5403,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":187,"executable":false,"size_bytes":6653,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"agents/openai.yaml","type":"yaml","lines":3,"executable":false,"size_bytes":313,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/stock_endpoints.json","type":"json","lines":16306,"executable":false,"size_bytes":431641,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/stock_endpoints.md","type":"markdown","lines":126,"executable":false,"size_bytes":14296,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"requirements.txt","type":"text","lines":4,"executable":false,"size_bytes":39,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/build_catalog.py","type":"python","lines":280,"executable":true,"size_bytes":8850,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/trading_analysis.py","type":"python","lines":577,"executable":true,"size_bytes":18581,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/tushare_stock.py","type":"python","lines":2283,"executable":true,"size_bytes":85035,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-ad679d8e66f146cd832a14df6841c768","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"声明描述的是一个面向A股使用场景的数据获取与分析型技能，听起来应当直接调用 Tushare 数据接口来获取股票数据，并进一步支持个股分析或交易观察。但给出的代码并未调用任何股票行情、财务或分析接口，也没有实现分析逻辑、观察逻辑或面向用户的查询功能。它做的事情是抓取 https://tushare.pro/document/2?doc_id=14 及其相关文档页面，解析接口说明、积分权限、参数表和返回字段，然后写出 references/stock_endpoints.json 和 stock_endpoints.md，属于“文档索引/元数据构建”脚本。虽然主题仍与 Tushare A 股接口相关，但主要用途与声明存在实质偏差，因此应判定为不匹配。","remediation":"Update the skill description to accurately reflect all capabilities, or remove undeclared functionality from the implementation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"code_path":"scripts/build_catalog.py","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":280,"actual_behavior_summary":"代码实际是一个离线构建脚本：抓取 Tushare 官方文档页面，解析股票数据接口目录、权限/积分说明、输入输出字段，并生成本地 JSON/Markdown 接口目录文件。"},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-ab742862f1e945a28743d63841dd9664","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":79,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/tushare_stock.py (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"python scripts/tushare_stock.py run --text \"<请求内容>\"","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"84ae4b6350d1d93017a9302f6d94cb05b6927f43fb8ee5d020e38fc13fde82d6","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":79,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-ab742862f1e945a28743d63841dd9664","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":127,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/tushare_stock.py (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"python scripts/tushare_stock.py run --text \"<请求内容>\"","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"84ae4b6350d1d93017a9302f6d94cb05b6927f43fb8ee5d020e38fc13fde82d6","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":127,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-ab742862f1e945a28743d63841dd9664","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":133,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/tushare_stock.py (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"python scripts/tushare_stock.py run --text \"<请求内容>\"","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"84ae4b6350d1d93017a9302f6d94cb05b6927f43fb8ee5d020e38fc13fde82d6","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":133,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-ab742862f1e945a28743d63841dd9664","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":139,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/tushare_stock.py (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"python scripts/tushare_stock.py run --text \"<请求内容>\"","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"84ae4b6350d1d93017a9302f6d94cb05b6927f43fb8ee5d020e38fc13fde82d6","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":139,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-ab742862f1e945a28743d63841dd9664","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":145,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/tushare_stock.py (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"python scripts/tushare_stock.py run --text \"<请求内容>\"","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"84ae4b6350d1d93017a9302f6d94cb05b6927f43fb8ee5d020e38fc13fde82d6","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":145,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-a1fc7e5d44534bdd834e3ed6535bdd8d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":1,"end_line":136},"finding":null,"explanation":"The entire skill description, examples, and interface guidance are presented only in Chinese, and the skill is framed specifically as a Chinese A-share research assistant without any opt-in or alternative language support. Under the policy, forcing a specific language or locale without user choice is a natural-language policy concern unless the constraint is explicitly justified as region-specific compliance or similar.","remediation":"Document that the skill is intentionally Chinese-language/China-market specific and why, or add explicit multilingual/user-choice wording such as offering Chinese by default with optional English interaction where supported.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":1,"end_line":136}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-5487a0ce6f7242e491e87c76d35524b9","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill declares environment, file, and network capabilities in metadata but does not define an explicit tool scope such as allowed-tools or permissions. That weakens least-privilege boundaries and can cause an agent runtime to grant broader access than users expect, especially since the skill can read a token, write cache files, and make outbound requests. In this context the behavior is not overtly malicious, but the missing scope increases risk if the skill is invoked in a permissive environment.","remediation":"Add explicit tool/permission declarations that narrowly scope what the skill may do: read only TUSHARE_TOKEN and the optional env file path, write only to a dedicated cache directory, and allow network access only to the documented Tushare domains. Document these permissions in the manifest and fail closed when the runtime cannot enforce them.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-337846875e8a47eb9c1178260d0bfecc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":156,"end_line":162},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown states that user-facing output '默认使用简体中文' and further instructs the skill to ask follow-up questions in Chinese when requests are unclear. This imposes a specific language/locale by default and does not offer the user a language choice or opt-in.","remediation":"Allow the skill to match the user's language automatically or explicitly document a user-selectable language option. For example, state that Chinese is the default for A-share workflows but English or other languages can be used on request.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":156,"end_line":162}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-384d6719622b459782b6a28d47070103","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":1685,"end_line":1822},"finding":null,"explanation":"Several endpoints in the catalog are specifically for 港股通, Hong Kong trading statistics, Hong Kong holdings, CCASS, and AH-share comparison, which are not limited to China A-shares. This is a semantic scope expansion relative to the manifest’s A-share-focused description.","remediation":"Remove Hong Kong and cross-border market endpoints from this skill, or revise the manifest to state that the skill also covers Hong Kong and cross-border stock-connect datasets.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":1685,"end_line":1822}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-6042de38c31b4d5ca5c74035eac3333b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":1845,"end_line":2199},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes a Tushare skill for Chinese A-shares, stock data, individual-stock analysis, and trading observation. However, the catalog explicitly exposes generic market interfaces whose documented parameters allow assets beyond A-shares, including Hong Kong/US markets, digital currency, futures, options, funds, and convertible bonds, which materially broadens the skill’s operational scope.","remediation":"Restrict the published catalog to A-share-relevant endpoints only, or update the manifest description to explicitly disclose the broader multi-asset and cross-market scope. If the broader endpoints must remain, gate or label them separately so callers can clearly distinguish non-A-share functionality.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":1845,"end_line":2199}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-b29c7db50f304ff78b7b87f88c6fd74e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":8673,"end_line":8677},"finding":null,"explanation":"Using the generic alias '股票开户数据' on one endpoint while another endpoint also claims it creates ambiguous routing behavior. Ambiguity in skill invocation is dangerous in agent systems because the model may select deprecated, inactive, or semantically different tools without user awareness.","remediation":"Ensure each alias uniquely identifies one endpoint. Remove the shared generic alias from deprecated or alternate endpoints and introduce explicit names like '股票开户数据（停）' and '股票开户数据（旧）' only.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":8673,"end_line":8677}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-b883c4ef5797482baf21dda09b3ddbf4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":8749,"end_line":8753},"finding":null,"explanation":"A second endpoint claiming the same broad alias increases collision risk and makes routing nondeterministic. This is particularly risky here because one endpoint is marked inactive/legacy, so ambiguous invocation can return stale or unexpected data and undermine user trust in analytical output.","remediation":"Deduplicate aliases across endpoints and block inactive or legacy endpoints from matching broad phrases. Require exact, versioned aliases for historical/old endpoints and prefer canonical identifiers in routing tables.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":8749,"end_line":8753}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-67d11c8696ae41d0a0e5ad2c7a4ac3f4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":12995,"end_line":12999},"finding":null,"explanation":"The generic alias '板块资金流向' lacks source or market constraints, making accidental or adversarial prompt steering more likely in NL-based routing. In a tool-using agent, ambiguous triggers can cause the wrong endpoint to fire and produce misleading analysis or unnecessary data access.","remediation":"Namespace aliases by provider and scope, such as including THS/DC and market/domain qualifiers. Enforce deterministic alias resolution and prompt the user to choose when multiple endpoints share similar meanings.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":12995,"end_line":12999}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-7eee790be13d42b59be52f5251c09f9a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":13297,"end_line":13300},"finding":null,"explanation":"Overly broad aliases can cause unintended skill or endpoint invocation, especially in an agent setting where natural-language routing is automatic. That can lead the system to query the wrong market dataset or perform actions with higher-cost, broader-scope, or less appropriate endpoints than the user intended.","remediation":"Replace generic aliases with scoped, unique trigger phrases that include market/source qualifiers. Add disambiguation logic requiring explicit user confirmation when an alias maps to multiple endpoints or broad financial concepts.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":13297,"end_line":13300}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-25fedf3772a64be398c7db4843d5f4cc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"scripts/trading_analysis.py","start_line":45,"end_line":49},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code hardcodes user-facing labels in Chinese, and the pattern continues throughout the file in conclusions, summaries, and limitations. Because the skill does not offer language selection or document that it is intentionally limited to a Chinese-speaking context, it violates the stated language/locale policy requirement.","remediation":"Add an explicit language/locale option so responses can be generated based on user preference, or clearly document that this skill is intended only for a Chinese-language/regional context and justify that constraint.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/trading_analysis.py","start_line":45,"end_line":49}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-84378161c22540c8b3c1117144e7bf9e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"scripts/tushare_stock.py","start_line":173,"end_line":268},"finding":null,"explanation":"Status strings and payload keys are systematically converted to Chinese, and all emitted JSON uses that localized structure. This is a natural-language locale policy concern because the file imposes a single language on users without any opt-in, fallback, or configuration choice.","remediation":"Add a language/locale option such as `--lang zh|en`, or default to neutral field names unless the user explicitly requests Chinese localization.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/tushare_stock.py","start_line":173,"end_line":268}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-464fd8d2dbb747bd945e40c1ef31ad8a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"scripts/tushare_stock.py","start_line":302,"end_line":304},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill accepts `TUSHARE_STOCK_ENV_FILE` and reads `TUSHARE_TOKEN` from an arbitrary local file path, enabling the process to read attacker-influenced files on disk if that environment variable is set unsafely by a caller or wrapper. In a skill environment, arbitrary local file reads exceed the stated stock-analysis purpose and can expose secrets or sensitive local configuration.","remediation":"Remove support for arbitrary env-file paths, or restrict reads to a fixed application-owned config directory with strict filename validation. Prefer reading credentials only from a dedicated environment variable or secret manager, and document any credential loading behavior to users/operators.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/tushare_stock.py","start_line":302,"end_line":304}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-88c02db8846244d38a410806286c6077","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":6,"end_line":16304},"finding":null,"explanation":"Natural-language content throughout the manifest is presented exclusively in Chinese, including user-facing titles and aliases, with no indication that users may choose another language. If this skill is intended for a broader user base, that constitutes a locale/language constraint without documented opt-in or justification.","remediation":"Document that the skill is Chinese-language only for a specific audience, or add multilingual aliases/descriptions and a user language selection mechanism.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":6,"end_line":16304}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-5d3aff818b3842c092301a51e71982b7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":3059,"end_line":3064},"finding":null,"explanation":"The entry is titled and named as a real-time ranking/list endpoint, and its output fields are ranking-style market snapshot fields across many stocks. Yet the description says it contains all intraday transaction records for a stock since market open, which describes tick-detail behavior instead of ranking behavior.","remediation":"Correct the description for realtime_list so it matches the actual endpoint purpose, e.g. describe it as a real-time ranked market list rather than per-stock tick-by-tick transaction data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":3059,"end_line":3064}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-eac1efe41198452a99d355540fe1071a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":8658,"end_line":8824},"finding":null,"explanation":"The stk_account and stk_account_old endpoints expose securities account-opening statistics, which are investor-account market structure data rather than stock-specific data retrieval, individual stock analysis, or trading observation. That capability is adjacent to market research but not clearly implied by the manifest’s narrower stock-oriented description.","remediation":"Either remove the account-opening endpoints from this skill or broaden the manifest description to mention investor participation / market structure statistics.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/stock_endpoints.json","start_line":8658,"end_line":8824}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-9e8a064dcb9145d99926f2dcdb94f777","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":"pandas","explanation":"The dependency list leaves pandas unpinned, so installs are not reproducible and may unexpectedly pull a vulnerable or breaking release in different environments or at different times. In a data-analysis skill that relies on third-party packages, this increases supply-chain risk and makes it difficult to verify whether known advisories apply.","remediation":"Pin pandas to a specific reviewed version or use constrained ranges with a lockfile (for example, requirements.txt plus pip-tools/poetry lock data). Regularly review upstream advisories and update the pinned version through a controlled dependency update process.","code_snippet":"pandas\ntushare\nrequests\nbeautifulsoup4","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"79cc545655ebca9f910a521d2c0057a53fee82e7690cc472ab749c517e08c398","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-29706b465e1c4d4391d296f5d2d1f21b","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: pandas has 1 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2020-13091 (** DISPUTED ** pandas through 1.0.3 can unserialize and execute commands from an)), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":"pandas","explanation":"Pandas has at least one known advisory, and because no version is pinned, it is impossible to determine from this manifest whether the deployed version is affected. This uncertainty is itself a security weakness because vulnerable versions may be installed silently, especially across different machines or over time.","remediation":"Pin pandas to a version confirmed not to be affected by known advisories, and document that version in a lockfile or constraints file. Add automated dependency scanning in CI to flag vulnerable versions before release.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9604ce04fc16a397c3c073b9e2bc539026bea65f4eab238f6f586124f40d1ff7","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-d37196ca609944ed86cd1f5fe015cd11","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":2,"end_line":null},"finding":"tushare","explanation":"The tushare dependency is unpinned, which means builds may resolve to different versions over time without review. For a finance-focused skill that consumes market data, inconsistent dependency resolution can introduce security, reliability, or integrity issues if a bad or compromised release is published.","remediation":"Pin tushare to a specific tested version and maintain a lockfile to ensure deterministic installs. Add dependency review in CI so version bumps are explicit, tested, and monitored for advisories or suspicious upstream changes.","code_snippet":"pandas\ntushare\nrequests\nbeautifulsoup4","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"da3c5f2bd6c592b9571e993692daedc5d64b94374d0a37c2da863aa3421098a6","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":2,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-c90159a100844bb194531429735a4f99","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":3,"end_line":null},"finding":"requests","explanation":"Requests is unpinned, so the environment may install an older vulnerable release or an unexpected newer release with security-impacting changes. Because this skill likely performs network access to retrieve stock data, the use of an unpinned HTTP client is somewhat more security-relevant than in a purely local tool.","remediation":"Pin requests to a known-safe version and use a lockfile for repeatable dependency resolution. Establish a process to promptly update the pinned version when security advisories are published and validate behavior in testing before deployment.","code_snippet":"pandas\ntushare\nrequests\nbeautifulsoup4","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6e256e7076a0cac063454c717f1df944a851308d6f40181450854ab6f7decb0a","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":3,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-03371c9be96a4583ab8b44ea00f01688","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: requests has 16 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2014-1830 (Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor in Requests); CVE-2024-47081 (Requests vulnerable to .netrc credentials leak via malicious URLs); CVE-2024-35195 (Requests `Session` object does not verify requests after making first request wi) +13 more), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":3,"end_line":null},"finding":"requests","explanation":"Requests has numerous historical advisories, and the lack of version pinning makes it unverifiable whether installation will select a safe release. In this skill's context, which likely performs outbound HTTP requests to fetch market data, a vulnerable requests version could expose credentials, weaken transport security, or mishandle malicious URLs.","remediation":"Pin requests to a current, reviewed version known to address published advisories and enforce it via a lockfile or constraints file. Integrate software composition analysis in CI/CD and regularly refresh the pin after testing security updates.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"09deeb6fdb55899e7b284b11a4a1f240e895ab350d9ef10d889ca4cada77cadd","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":3,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-0c1f775e64164144a6a14de4f3519b7b","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":4,"end_line":null},"finding":"beautifulsoup4\n","explanation":"BeautifulSoup4 is unpinned, creating non-reproducible installations and avoidable supply-chain uncertainty. Even though parsing libraries are often lower risk than direct execution components, unexpected version changes can still introduce vulnerable transitive dependencies or unsafe parsing behavior.","remediation":"Pin beautifulsoup4 to a reviewed version and generate a lockfile to make installs deterministic. Periodically audit both direct and transitive dependencies and update pins through a controlled release process.","code_snippet":"pandas\ntushare\nrequests\nbeautifulsoup4","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"b352dbf0f80961594ef5aa722f159040767884cc2997f1c9988967e86e0267cb","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":4,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-bdbd6df14c374e38be2b44ae039d5339","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"scripts/build_catalog.py","start_line":147,"end_line":149},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes a Tushare skill for obtaining and analyzing A-share stock data, which suggests runtime data-access and analysis capabilities. This script instead crawls Tushare documentation pages and generates local reference artifacts, which is a repository-maintenance behavior not reflected in the stated skill description.","remediation":"Clarify in the manifest or developer documentation that the repository includes a documentation-catalog build step, or separate this script from the shipped skill code so the skill description only covers code used for the declared stock-data functionality.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/build_catalog.py","start_line":147,"end_line":149}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-28aab10db34e407cb0d04d5d46214840","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"scripts/build_catalog.py","start_line":257,"end_line":274},"finding":null,"explanation":"The stated purpose focuses on stock data retrieval, analysis, and trading observation for A-shares. Creating a references directory and writing JSON/Markdown catalog files is a build/documentation generation task, which does not match that user-facing description.","remediation":"Document this offline catalog-generation behavior as part of the skill's maintenance tooling, or move it into a separate developer-only utility outside the skill's described functional scope.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/build_catalog.py","start_line":257,"end_line":274}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1dd3e061db904c41b11d0a054938307b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"scripts/tushare_stock.py","start_line":298,"end_line":305},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code accesses sensitive credentials via `TUSHARE_TOKEN` and optionally reads the same secret from a user-specified env file. There is no confirmation prompt, user-facing warning, or nearby comment/docstring disclosing that credential material will be accessed.","remediation":"Add a brief user-visible warning or documentation note that the script reads `TUSHARE_TOKEN` from the environment or from `TUSHARE_STOCK_ENV_FILE`, and clarify that users should provide a token file only if they intend the skill to access it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/tushare_stock.py","start_line":298,"end_line":305}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b89dd24acc5846e2ba5a9dfe0dae62a5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/tushare_stock.py","start_line":318,"end_line":322},"finding":null,"explanation":"Initializing `ts.pro_api(token)` enables subsequent outbound API requests, and the script later sends stock codes, dates, and natural-language-derived query parameters to the remote Tushare service. The file contains no visible disclosure to users that their requests trigger external network access to a third-party data provider.","remediation":"Add a user-facing notice in CLI help text, star